      "tag_id": "Kesehatan",
      "tag_en": "Health",
      "title_id": "Manfaat Renang untuk Kesehatan Fisik dan Mental",
      "title_en": "Benefits of Swimming for Physical and Mental Health",
      "excerpt_id": "Renang bukan cuma olahraga kardio. Ini yang terjadi pada tubuh dan pikiranmu setiap kali rutin berenang.",
      "excerpt_en": "Swimming is more than a cardio workout. Here's what happens to your body and mind when you swim regularly.",
      "slug": "manfaat-renang-kesehatan",
      "image": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
      "body_id": "Renang sering disebut olahraga yang paling lengkap. Berikut alasan kenapa banyak orang menjadikannya kebiasaan rutin.\n\n## Melatih seluruh tubuh\nSaat berenang, hampir semua kelompok otot ikut bekerja: lengan, bahu, punggung, perut, hingga kaki.\n\n## Ramah untuk sendi\nKarena air menopang berat tubuh, renang tergolong olahraga low-impact yang lebih nyaman untuk sendi dibanding olahraga berdampak tinggi.\n\n## Melatih kebugaran jantung dan napas\nBerenang secara rutin dapat membantu meningkatkan stamina dan kontrol pernapasan.\n\n## Membantu pikiran lebih rileks\nGerakan berirama dan sensasi di dalam air membuat banyak orang merasa lebih tenang setelah berenang.\n\n## Keterampilan hidup\nLebih dari sekadar olahraga, kemampuan berenang adalah life skill yang berguna sepanjang hidup — itulah alasan HUCAS percaya: Learn to Swim. Learn for Life.\n\nBelum bisa berenang? Tidak masalah, semua bisa belajar. Lihat program kami di website ini.",
      "body_en": "Swimming is often called one of the most complete forms of exercise. Here's why so many people make it a regular habit.\n\n## Works your whole body\nWhile swimming, almost every major muscle group is engaged: arms, shoulders, back, core and legs.\n\n## Gentle on the joints\nBecause water supports your body weight, swimming is a low-impact exercise that is easier on the joints than high-impact sports.\n\n## Builds cardio fitness and breath control\nSwimming regularly can help improve stamina and breathing control.\n\n## Helps the mind relax\nThe rhythmic movement and the feel of the water leave many people feeling calmer after a swim.\n\n## A life skill\nMore than exercise, swimming is a life skill that stays useful for life — which is why HUCAS believes: Learn to Swim. Learn for Life.\n\nCan't swim yet? No problem, everyone can learn. Check out our programs on this website."
